<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating interval probabilities and expected frequencies for a uniform distribution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A commercial bakery in Nakuru produces loaves of bread. Due to slight variations in the dough mixing process, the exact weight \(W\) of a standard loaf is <b>uniformly distributed</b> between <b>{@a@}g</b> and <b>{@b@}g</b>.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> The bakery's quality control standards require a loaf to weigh <b>at least {@c@}g</b> to be approved for sale to supermarkets. Calculate the probability that a randomly selected loaf meets this standard.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fully simplified fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> During the morning shift, the bakery produces a batch of <b>{@N@} loaves</b>. Based on your probability from part (a), calculate the <b>expected number</b> of loaves from this batch that will be approved for supermarket sale.</p>
<p>\(\text{Expected loaves} =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Quality Control Probability</b><br>
The total width of the uniform distribution is \(b - a = {@b@} - {@a@} = {@w@}\).</p>
<p>We want the probability that the weight is at least \({@c@}\)g, which corresponds to the interval from \({@c@}\)g up to the maximum weight of \({@b@}\)g:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(W \ge {@c@}) = \frac{b - c}{b - a} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(W \ge {@c@}) = \frac{{@b@} - {@c@}}{{@w@}} = \frac{{@b - c@}}{{@w@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(W \ge {@c@}) = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Expected Frequency</b><br>
The expected frequency (\(E\)) of an event is found by multiplying the total number of trials (\(N\)) by the probability of the event occurring (\(p\)):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle E = N \times P(W \ge {@c@}) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle E = {@N@} \times {@ta1@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ E = {@ta2@} \text{ loaves} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
